The race condition is where multiple threads evaluate the if statement as true and they all
try to construct the _context object. All will succeed, but they will overwrite the
previously constructed value by doing so. Of course, this is inefficient, especially when the
constructor is a costly operation, but the issue discovered with the unit test is that
the _context object is actually constructed by a thread after another thread or threads
have updated the books collection. That is why the books collection, _books, has a different
number of elements between runs.
