Unlike the previous example, the container that is generated is an instance of
Autofac.IContainer. This will be used to retrieve each registered
dependency. QuitCommand, for example, will be named both "q" and "quit", which
indicates the two commands that can be used to execute the command. Also, note the last
registered type is not named, and belongs to UnknownCommand. This will act as a default if
no command is found by name.
To determine a dependency, a new method will be used to retrieve the dependency by
name:
public InventoryCommand GetCommand(string input)
{
return
Container.ResolveOptionalNamed<InventoryCommand>(input.ToLower()) ??
Container.Resolve<InventoryCommand>();
}
